nceVYKSzRd__lF","title":"spectralOrdering(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","role":"symbol","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"spectralOrdering"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":" = false, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-8, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","text":"NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"] "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz","text":"BinaryInteger"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Every weight is finite and nonnegative, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}]}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" matrix–vector","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver answers and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached the default limits in the measurements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The spectral ordering (Barnard, Pothen and Simon): the components in order of their least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index; a component of at most two vertices in index order; a larger one ascending by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the Fiedler vector of that component (for a connected graph, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fiedlerVector()"},{"type":"text","text":"’s), entries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within 10⁻⁸ · max|x| of their predecessor kept in index order. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[]"},{"type":"text","text":" for the empty graph."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/spectralordering(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)-4odqr"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/spectralOrdering(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)-4odqr","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The error an iterative method throws when it uses up its iteration limit without meeting its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stopping rule.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","title":"NoConvergence","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","role":"symbol"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Spect